  "modified": "2026-09-02T19:56:20Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-33818: enforce a maximum recursion depth in encoding/asn1 Unmarshal\n  to prevent stack exhaustion when parsing deeply-nested recursive structures\n- CVE-2026-56853: apply ReadHeaderTimeout to the server's unencrypted HTTP/2\n  client preface check, and clear the connection timeouts again once the\n  connection is handed off to the http2 package\n- CVE-2026-56858: fix JavaScript regexp context tracking in html/template so\n  that pathological input can no longer close an unescaped '/' early and\n  inject attacker-controlled content\n- CVE-2026-56859: add a recursion depth guard during decode in encoding/xml so\n  that DecodeElement no longer resets the depth counter, preventing stack\n  exhaustion\n- CVE-2026-56860: avoid quadratic complexity in net/url resolvePath by\n  resolving '..' segments with index-based backtracking on a byte buffer\n- CVE-2026-56862: do not count handshake messages as state-advancing after the\n  handshake has completed in crypto/tls, bounding the key derivation work a\n  client can force with repeated KeyUpdate messages",
